    <string name="tutorial_title">BENCH TRAINING</string>
    <string name="tutorial_caption">STEP %1$d OF %2$d</string>
    <string name="tutorial_next">NEXT</string>
    <string name="tutorial_title_1">THE BENCH DRAINS</string>
    <string name="tutorial_body_1">The peg field pushes the token outward. Left alone it drifts to the dead gutters at the edges and pays nothing.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_title_2">MOVE THE GATES</string>
    <string name="tutorial_body_2">Three deflector gates sit on the field. Drag one into the lane the token will cross, press it to turn its facing, and the token follows it.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_title_3">SPEND TORQUE</string>
    <string name="tutorial_body_3">Every lane step and every turn costs one torque pip. RESET parks the gates and gives the pips back for this round.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_title_4">CALIBRATE</string>
    <string name="tutorial_body_4">Between rounds four pads flash a sequence. Repeat it to refill torque and earn a payout bonus. Miss it and the bench loses stability.</string>
